refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public static Time\DurationTime\Duration::fromMinutes intminutes
Creates a non-negative duration of minutes minutes. The value is normalized into whole seconds and nanoseconds, see the Time\Duration::$seconds and Time\Duration::$nanoseconds properties.

&reftitle.parameters;
minutes
The number of minutes. Must be greater than or equal to 0.

&reftitle.errors;



   If minutes is negative, a
   ValueError is thrown.


 &ext.datetime.duration-too-long;

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::fromMinutes example


<?php
var_dump(\Time\Duration::fromMinutes(90));

try {
    \Time\Duration::fromMinutes(-1);
} catch (ValueError $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


